{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/sfaxgred","slide":2,"text":"A model is one component—not the decision-maker.","textPreview":"A model is one component—not the decision-maker.","textChars":48,"textLines":1,"bbox":[58,530,560,52]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gvxj9c","slide":2,"text":"The central idea is simple. National intelligence must integrate evidence, uncertainty, authority, and action. The five controls shown here are Integrated evidence, Surveillance, Capacity, Equity, Accountability. Together, they prevent a health signal from being mistaken for an authorized decision.\n\n[Sources]\n- Canonical notebook V7_B_N15, SRAI Book 7 v1.0."}
